The implementation specified in [PRD.md](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/PRD.md) and [plan.md](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/plan.md) has been built in `/opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead`.

---

### 1. What Was Built

- **Containerized WAHA Service**: Loopback-isolated Docker Compose config (`127.0.0.1:3000`) for WhatsApp Webhook ingestion.
- **WAHA Session Management**: Script to initialize the `default` session with HMAC-SHA512 signing, exponential retries (5 attempts, 2s delay), and QR code retrieval instructions for test pairing.
- **n8n Scoring Pipeline**: Complete rebuilt workflow (`active: false`) containing the exact 10 nodes:
  1. [`WhatsApp Webhook`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (`POST /webhook/wa-hotlead`)
  2. [`Verify HMAC`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (Recomputes HMAC-SHA512 over payload, verifies `X-Webhook-Hmac`, rejects on mismatch)
  3. [`Normalize & Dedupe`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (Normalizes fields, strips `@c.us`, dedupes against local JSONL store by `payload.id`)
  4. [`Load Conversation Context`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (Reconstructs last 20 messages per sender with `Cust:` / `Biz:` tags)
  5. [`Score Lead (ID Rules)`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (Bahasa Indonesia dictionary scoring with `warm >= 20`, `hot >= 60`, and intent-question boost)
  6. [`Is Hot?`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (Branches on `lead_level == hot`)
  7. [`Notify Sales (Hot)`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (Builds alert `{sender} HOT ({score}): {message}`)
  8. [`Send QualifiedLead to Meta (disabled)`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (`disabled: true`, placeholder for Pixel ID/token and hashed PII)
  9. [`Log Warm/Cold`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/n8n/workflow-wa-hotlead.json) (Logs non-hot leads)
  10. `Sticky: Flow Notes` (Architectural flow documentation)
- **Scoring Rules & Prompts**: Bahasa keyword dictionary with corrected threshold (`warm: 20`) and LLM fallback prompt for JSON classification.
- **Operator Runbook & REST Importer**: [`README.md`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/README.md) runbook and [`scripts/import-workflow.sh`](file:///opt/data/projects/wa-hot-lead/scripts/import-workflow.sh) to import the workflow into n8n without auto-activating.

